      {
        "id": 65153,
        "name": "rkcr",
        "username": "rkcr",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/b5ac83/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-06T17:29:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Kingofsouls\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Kingofsouls:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Anyway you can add HP trackers to this?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I could, but I've been against it so far. &nbsp;The core problem is that I don't personally want one. &nbsp;Having a centralized repository of HP info is not as much fun as tossing little tokens around the table. &nbsp;Plus SotM is already susceptible to being a one-player coop game, so having everyone have to figure out HP themselves helps alleviate that.</p>\n<p>Maybe there's another use case I'm not thinking of, though.</p>",
